-- title:
--   A primitive q-th root of unity on each component of the H₁ moduli ring
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and naturals $\ell_g, M'$ with $\ell_g$ prime, $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$, $M' \neq 0$, $q \nmid M'$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$. Let $A_0$ be a discrete valuation domain with finite residue field whose maximal ideal is generated by $q$, and in which $\ell_g$ and $M'$ are units. Assume three transport hypotheses: `hℓ`, that for every $A_0$-algebra $T$, Weierstrass curve $W/T$ and variable change $C$, the conditions defining a $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-point (the pair $(x_P,y_P)$ satisfies the affine equation, $\mathrm{pre}\Psi_{\ell_g}$ vanishes at $x_P$, and $(x_Q,y_Q)=(x_P,y_P)$) are carried by $C$ to the transformed level datum; `hM`, that the $\Gamma_0(p^k)$-condition `IsGamma0PowAt` (the two-torsion kernel condition when $p^k=2$, otherwise the cyclic generator-kernel conditions on $h$) is preserved by `kernelVariableChangeDeg`; and `hL`, that divisibility of `inLineMulPoly W ℓg n x` by $h$ is preserved under the same substitution. Let $\mathcal{G}$ be a family of relative group laws on the projective models of discriminant-unit curves over $A_0$-algebras, satisfying the chord–tangent condition (existence of an addition- and Galois-compatible identification of sections over fields with affine points) and the origin-identity condition (the unit section is cut out by a chart homomorphism killing $x/y$ and $z/y$), and let $\mathcal{T}$ be a level transport for $(\mathcal{G},q)$ on raw Drinfeld pairs, compatible with sections under variable changes and coefficient homomorphisms. Assume further that variable changes and $A_0$-algebra maps are realised by graded ring homomorphisms between the projective-model graded rings satisfying `IsVariableChangeHom`, respectively `IsCoefficientHom`, and dominating the irrelevant ideal. Let $P_0$ be an abstract fine moduli package for the level moduli datum attached to `rigidDataH1Pow A₀ ℓg M' q …` — points over $T$ being variable-change classes of tuples consisting of a discriminant-unit curve, a generator-kernel polynomial for each prime factor of $M'$, a $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-point whose $x$-coordinate is linked to the $\ell_g$-component polynomial via `IsGamma1Link`, and a Drinfeld basis of level $q$ — so that $P_0.B_0$ is an $A_0$-algebra carrying a universal point through which every point over every $A_0$-algebra factors by a unique $A_0$-algebra homomorphism; assume $P_0.B_0$ is of finite type over $A_0$. Then for every minimal prime $\mathfrak{P}$ of the zero ideal of $P_0.B_0$ there is $b \in P_0.B_0$ whose image in $P_0.B_0/\mathfrak{P}$ is a primitive $q$-th root of unity.
--
--   This records the classical fact that the $q$-th roots of unity appear in the $\Gamma(q)$-level moduli ring, via the Weil pairing of the universal Drinfeld basis: on each irreducible component of the $H_1$ fine moduli ring the value $e_q(P,Q)$ is a primitive $q$-th root of $1$ and is already represented by an element of the ring. It feeds the comparison of completions of the moduli ring at primes over $q$ and the classification of points with values in the base.
